        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "xcOLA",
          "x": 203,
          "y": 4902,
          "name": "Panel Menus",
          "theme": {
            "mode": "dark"
          },
          "clip": true,
          "width": 2100,
          "fill": "$ds-bg",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 30,
          "padding": [
            48,
            40
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "eFKeY",
              "name": "Header",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 10,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "TlaIH",
                  "name": "Kicker",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg-subtle",
                  "content": "MENUS",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "600",
                  "letterSpacing": 1.5
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "HnwdZ",
                  "name": "Title",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg",
                  "content": "Every panel carries its own menus",
                  "lineHeight": 1.05,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-display",
                  "fontSize": 44,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "B8NHua",
                  "name": "Sub",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1240,
                  "content": "A panel can open a menu on its left and on its right, toggled from its own tab strip and closable independently. They belong to the panel — the session's Context files and Run parameters travel with the session, whatever slot it sits in. That is exactly why resource navigation cannot live in one, and needs its own space in the sidenav.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "ZY9zw",
              "name": "Anatomy",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "fill": "$ds-bg-subtle",
              "cornerRadius": 12,
              "stroke": "$ds-border",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "strokeAlignment": "inner",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 14,
              "padding": 20,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "UEzXp",
                  "name": "T",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg",
                  "content": "Panel anatomy",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "MXjK9",
                  "name": "D",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "Tabs and the “+” sit on the left of the strip. A menu's icon appears only when that menu is closed — an open menu needs no toggle, because it is already there and closes from its own header. Closed, the icon opens the menu as a dropdown instead, and the dropdown's header reattaches it. Each menu registers its own icon.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "H4seV",
                  "name": "N",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg-subtle",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "The menus belong to the panel, not the slot — bubblify the session into a floating panel and Context files goes with it, icon and all. This is also the reason the sidenav needs a resource region: navigating a workspace's children is not a panel action, so no panel menu can own it.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "LyjfL",
                  "name": "Panels",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "gap": 16,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "PMQkK",
                      "name": "Both open",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 8,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "YJO6R",
                          "name": "L",
                          "fill": "$ds-review",
                          "content": "both menus attached · no icons in the strip",
                          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                          "fontSize": 11,
                          "fontWeight": "600"
                        },
